==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{bor+|en|de|Sudetenland}}, named after the [[Sudeten]] mountain range, but encompassing a far greater area.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/suˈdeɪ̯tənˌlænd/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-Sudetenland.ogg|a=US}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{lb|en|historical}} The northern, southern{{,}} and western border areas of former [[Czechoslovakia]], which (until 1945) were inhabited mainly by German-speakers

